WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.532
Planning begins with the learner and the work they need to perform.

2
00:00:04.532 --> 00:00:13.515
Define the audience, prior knowledge, learning objectives, course length, tone, delivery format, and completion requirements.

3
00:00:13.515 --> 00:00:17.723
A course for new employees may need more context and examples.

4
00:00:17.723 --> 00:00:23.307
A refresher for experienced staff may need shorter modules and stronger job aids.

5
00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:27.596
Production choices should follow those instructional needs.

6
00:00:27.596 --> 00:00:34.475
Storyboards, scripts, narration plans, visual briefs, and asset lists keep production organized.

7
00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:36.984
A storyboard maps the learning flow.

8
00:00:36.984 --> 00:00:39.412
A script explains what will be said.

9
00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:44.024
A visual brief describes the purpose of each graphic or media asset.

10
00:00:44.024 --> 00:00:52.360
An asset list tracks what must be created, who owns it, what format is needed, and whether it has been reviewed and approved.

11
00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.325
Separate instructional content from production assets.

12
00:00:56.325 --> 00:00:59.967
The content explains what learners need to know or do.

13
00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:07.331
The asset pipeline defines the visuals, audio, video, documents, and exports needed to teach that content.

14
00:01:07.331 --> 00:01:16.314
This distinction helps teams avoid treating every paragraph as a graphic request or every graphic as a substitute for explanation.

15
00:01:16.314 --> 00:01:21.413
Naming conventions and folder structure are practical quality controls.

16
00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:26.187
Use file names that identify module, asset type, version, and status.

17
00:01:26.187 --> 00:01:29.020
Keep source files separate from exports.

18
00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.876
Track approved versions and avoid overwriting final assets casually.

19
00:01:33.876 --> 00:01:42.616
Even a small course can become difficult to revise when images, audio, scripts, and exports are scattered or ambiguously named.

20
00:01:42.616 --> 00:01:53.784
Decide constraints early: screen size, brand style, accessibility expectations, caption requirements, file size limits, LMS constraints, and export targets.

21
00:01:53.784 --> 00:01:55.969
Those decisions reduce rework.

22
00:01:55.969 --> 00:02:08.917
If a course will use 16:9 screens, responsive layouts, SCORM tracking, downloadable PDFs, and captioned videos, those facts should influence the asset pipeline before production begins.
